% References for the MECH5720 report. The paper entries were checked against Crossref, DOI records or
% the authors' own pages in October 2026. Web pages, datasheets and manuals sit at the end. The brief
% asks for papers in the literature review, so cite the web entries in the method alone.
%
% IEEE format with the stock IEEEtran.bst (the ICCP template):
%  - Journal and conference names use the IEEE abbreviations.
%  - Conference entries carry the venue city in address and no publisher, so they print as
%    "in Proc. ..., City, Country, Mon. year, pp. x-y".
%  - IEEEtran.bst ignores the doi field, so each note repeats the DOI as "doi: ...". The doi field stays
%    for other tools.
%  - IEEEtran.bst lowercases the first letter of a note. Wrap that first word in braces to keep its case.
%  - IEEEtran.bst turns every hyphen in pages into an en dash. Write a hyphen inside a page number as {\char45}.
%  - Web sources take the link in url, which prints as "[Online]. Available:". The access date goes at the end of
%    howpublished, since IEEE puts a full stop before "Accessed:" and IEEEtran.bst puts a comma before a note.
%  - The control entry below stops IEEEtran.bst replacing a repeated author with a dash. main.tex loads it
%    with stctlcite.

@IEEEtranBSTCTL{IEEEexample:BSTcontrol,
  CTLdash_repeated_names = "no"
}

